# Frontend — Next.js + shadcn (apps & packages)

## Stack (decided)

- **Framework:** Next.js (**App Router**).
- **UI:** **shadcn/ui** (Radix primitives + Tailwind) — copy components into the repo, customize in place.
- **Styling:** Tailwind CSS (required for shadcn).

## SEO (marketing & public pages)

- Use the **Metadata API** (`metadata` export or `generateMetadata`) for title, description, Open Graph, canonical URLs.
- Prefer **server components** for indexable content; keep critical copy and headings in server-rendered HTML (not only inside client-only islands).
- Mind **Core Web Vitals**: sensible image formats (`next/image`), avoid blocking the main thread on first paint for hero sections.
- Public routes should have a clear heading hierarchy (`h1` once per page, logical `h2`/`h3`).

## Dashboard / product routes

- Authenticated flows: generation UI, history, settings — SEO is secondary; client components are fine where interactivity dominates.
- **Never** embed GPU inference in the browser for production; call **FastAPI** (same patterns as `client.py`: JSON + Base64 image).

## Calling the inference API

- Use **`NEXT_PUBLIC_*`** only for **non-secret** values (e.g. public API base URL in dev). Secrets belong in **Route Handlers** (`app/api/.../route.ts`) or server actions that proxy to FastAPI server-side.
- Forward **`X-Request-ID`** or generate a client correlation id when debugging (optional).

## Structure hints

- Colocate feature UI under `app/(marketing)/`, `app/(dashboard)/` or similar **route groups** to separate layouts without duplicating Next apps.
- Shared primitives live in `components/ui/` (shadcn) and composables in `components/` — extract duplicates instead of copying between marketing and dashboard.

## Testing (when the web app exists)

- **API client logic:** test parsing of success and **error** payloads (`error_code`, `request_id`) so UI matches FastAPI behavior.
- **E2E smoke:** one happy path + one failure path (e.g. 429 or timeout) is enough for early MVP; expand as the product stabilizes.
- Prefer **Playwright** (or equivalent) for browser E2E; keep tests independent of real GPU by mocking at the HTTP boundary or using a dedicated test API when available.

## What not to do

- Do not add FastAPI or Python under `apps/`.
- Do not ship API keys or admin tokens in `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` env vars.
